Hi Michael,

Could you approve the R02 slides and the attached figure for the oral talk at=
 the Applied Document Research Forum? In yesterday's read-through, Emily hear=
d the gain before she heard which run we were comparing against. I've moved t=
he evaluation set and the two run conditions ahead of the figure.

I'll start with the case-based split and the same 1,200 evaluation documents =
for both runs. Joshua reported on July 7 that no cases were shared between an=
y pair of partitions. Fatima and I reconciled the document totals and checked=
 the scoring against the common reference labels. We had Joshua's report on t=
he overlap and lacked the case-level allocation detail to repeat his check.

Before showing the figure, I'll explain that both runs use the same training =
documents and one top intent per received body. R173 uses word frequencies. R=
184 adds character 3=E2=80=935 grams. The figure uses a zero-to-one scale. I'=
ll say that R184 scored 0.873 against R173's 0.852, a difference of 0.021 in =
macro-F1 on this evaluation, with all 12 intents weighted equally. I'll menti=
on that Reschedule fell from 0.888 to 0.829 so the average doesn't suggest a =
gain in every intent.

I'm asking to project the deck and figure in the room. I'll keep the frozen r=
esults PDF and the separate comparison TSV internal for your review. I'll lea=
ve out examples of intake text and keep any questions about adopting the mode=
l for routing separate from the research result.

Thanks,
Vanessa

